# Rust
/target/

# Node
node_modules/
app/dist/

# Dev vault (cargo run -- serve ./devvault). Unanchored on purpose: a second
# devvault/ anywhere in the tree makes that command mean different things from
# different directories, because cargo finds Cargo.toml by walking up while the
# path argument stays relative to where you are standing.
devvault/

# VAULT_PATH is required now and compose refuses to start without it, so nothing
# should land here again. Kept because the folder may already exist in a working
# copy from before that changed, and because a real vault appearing inside the
# checkout is the one mistake that ends with someone's notes in a public repo.
deploy/vault/

# Someone's real VAULT_PATH, and on Linux their uid. `deploy/.env.example` is the
# checked-in one.
deploy/.env

# OS
.DS_Store

# cargo-mutants' scratch trees and report (ADR-006). Regenerated every run and
# large; the report that matters is the CI job summary and its artifact.
mutants.out/
